// prelude/conv — number <-> string conversion.
//
//   atoi(s) -> int   parse a signed decimal integer (skips leading spaces,
//                    accepts an optional leading '-')
//
// The reverse direction (itoa) is provided by `print`/`println`, which format
// an int argument in decimal and write it to stdout.
int main() {
    println(atoi("42"));
    println(atoi("-17") * 2);
    int x = atoi("  100");
    println(x + atoi("23"));
    return 0;
}
